# TESTING (THIN)

Zero bloat in tests. Prefer observable behavior at stable boundaries; direct tests of critical internal invariants (authorization, parsing, migrations, concurrency, recovery) allowed. Native tools (`Read`/`Grep`/`Write`/`StrReplace`).
Run the verify this change can break. Fail closed on red; report pre-existing/env blockers, do not loop forever. Cite evidence (command, exit, scope).
Docs or NOW.md only: no house gauntlet. Hooks, scripts, or tests: `bash tests/run.sh` and `bash scripts/doctor.sh`. Trusted workspace: run those fixtures without asking.
Bug fix ships `regression: <symptom>` with observed fail-before/pass-after; the label alone is not proof. Flaky = broken.

Coverage of the defined change scope (diff vs merge-base/HEAD, worktree+index, or named files where tooling supports it; else state scope + residual) is **100%** when the repo already has a coverage job — cite that job; risk-based, genuine exclusions ok. Coverage is evidence, not proof of correctness. Do not add a coverage runner. Whole-repo 100% is not a reason to test getters or mock internals.
Mutation: if the repo already runs a mutator, **0 meaningful surviving mutants** on files you touched; investigate survivors; equivalent/irrelevant needs explicit justification. Do not add Stryker, PIT, or mutmut.

## PROCEDURE
TDD order, mocks, gauntlet workflows:
**Read `~/.cursor/skills/testing/SKILL.md`** when writing or expanding a test workflow, not before a one-line assertion.
